    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Plate movement is driven by heat generated inside the Earth, which produces convection currents in the mantle.",
      "id": "mgb8nsz"
    },
    {
      "id": "rw2r2qy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Characteristics of Lithospheric Plates"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Plate tectonics refined Wegener’s ideas by demonstrating that continents and ocean floors move together as lithospheric plates.",
        "Lithospheric plates float over the asthenosphere, a mechanically weak and partially molten layer.",
        "Internal heat from the Earth generates convection currents in the mantle that drive plate movement.",
        "Plate interiors are relatively stable, whereas plate boundaries are geologically active."
      ],
      "id": "yl2dumq"
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Plate tectonics refined Wegener’s ideas by explaining that both continents and ocean floors move together as parts of lithospheric plates.",
      "id": "momuti0"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Average thickness ranges from 50 to 150 km.",
      "id": "0xr27kk"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Plates may consist of oceanic crust, continental crust, or both.",
      "id": "mzy3b7i"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Plate velocities typically range from 2 to 10 cm per year.",
      "id": "y90plvl"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Plate interiors are relatively stable, while boundaries are geologically active.",
      "id": "kxwrys6"
    },
    {
