      "items": [
        "Lithospheric plates float over the asthenosphere, which is defined as a mechanically weak and partially molten zone.",
        "The primary driving force of plate motion is heat-generated convection currents in the mantle.",
        "Average plate thickness (50–150 km) and movement velocity (2–10 cm/year) are frequently tested parameters.",
        "Geological activity is concentrated at plate boundaries, while plate interiors remain stable."
      ],
      "id": "xm95q8w"
